# graphify knowledge graph — paths here are relative to this folder.
#
# GRAPH_REPORT.md and manifest.json ARE committed on purpose: the point is that
# everyone (and every agent) starts from the same map, and the post-commit hook
# keeps them current for free (AST only, no API cost).
#
# graph.json is NOT, as of 2026-08-31. It is 5.2MB of generated JSON that the
# hook rewrites after every code commit, and clustering reshuffles communities
# even when the node and edge counts are identical — so it arrived as a
# multi-thousand-line diff on unrelated commits, went stale on any branch that
# was not rebuilt, and needed a merge driver to survive parallel work. It is
# derived data: `graphify update .` rebuilds it from the AST in under a minute,
# with no API key and no cost.
#
# What makes that cheap is that .graphify_labels.json IS still committed, so a
# local rebuild reuses the prose community names rather than falling back to
# bare filenames. Fresh clone: run `graphify update .` once (see AGENTS.md).
#
# Local-only below:
graph.json

# Per-machine interpreter/root pointers.
.graphify_python
.graphify_root

# Rebuildable in seconds, and 2MB+ of churn per commit.
graph.html
cache/
cost.json

# Intermediate extraction sidecars, but KEEP .graphify_analysis.json — the
# report and the community labels are derived from it.
.graphify_ast.json
.graphify_semantic.json
.graphify_extract.json
.graphify_detect.json
.graphify_chunk_*.json
.graphify_cached.json
.graphify_uncached.txt
.graphify_semantic_new.json

# Dated backups of the curated graph, written automatically on every rebuild
# (~5MB each). The post-commit hook rebuilds on every code commit, so these
# accumulate daily. graph.json is committed and its history is in git already,
# which is the actual safety net; these are a local undo buffer.
20[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]/

# Transient lock written while a hook-triggered rebuild is in flight.
.rebuild.lock
